      <revisionDesc>
         <change when="2026-03-16T12:53:39-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Finalized - done</change>
         <change when="2026-03-15T13:06:15-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Vote - Accept-Straight-to-Finalization - Fine with the corrections to lines 11 and 17. In lin19 πόλιν is not strictly necessary, and ]φ is part of an abbreviation, not a number. I correct this and other passages in P.Oxy. LXXXVIII 5672.2 n.</change>
         <change when="2026-03-15T11:21:21-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Submit - A few new corrections.</change>
         <change when="2026-03-15T11:20:56-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - A few corrections (but there's more to be done with the text): lin3 I've tacitly changed κατατρέχοντα to \κα/τατρέχοντα; lin11 [.?]λ̣ο̣τ̣ο̣ν̣τ̣ο̣ν̣ =&gt; [.?] κ̣ἂν νῦν, a common expression but usually with an Imperative (cf. Di Bartolo 2021: 66). Reading an infinitive ἐξαποστῖλαι without dotting the right half of the word is too bold; lin17 the pap. has χρόνου not χρόνῳ. It could be useful to restore the participle δεδραμι-κότι (l. δεδραμηκότι). The word doesn't look abbreviated; lin19 φ doesn't appear to be a number but it has a cross stroke, suggesting it's an abbreviated word. </change>
